Subject: Cantor M2B Post Supplied Ordered Topology Inventory Digest Architecture Review

Description: Between-slice review after exact supplied ordered-sequence commitment is proven. It selects one zero-effect reconciliation of two complete output-only digest carriers while keeping observation order, physical timing, inventory completeness, quiescence, receipt, admission, and every effect outside the selected boundary.

@ [topology_forms] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Machine_Forms.sop
@ [scanner_formation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner.sop
@ [digest_authority] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_M2B_Supplied_Ordered_Topology_Inventory_Digest.sop
@ [digest_proof] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_M2B_Supplied_Ordered_Topology_Inventory_Digest_Proof.sop
@ [seal_formation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Candidate_Seal_And_Independent_Review.sop

& [ReviewIdentity] is exact
  + [review_uuid] is 72a52fd6-26f5-4eff-a554-3c9efec20ce1
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [baseline_commit] is 4193fa1bc51f586d795817cc56b115064cccf4f6
  + [status] is checkpoint_complete_next_pure_boundary_selected

& [ClosedSupport] is exact
  + one complete supplied assembly owns a bounded root-first ordered carrier sequence
  + current topology and assembly correlations are rerun before commitment
  + one explicit versioned byte grammar commits every observation and stream semantic field
  + one streaming SHA-256 produces an architecture-independent sequence commitment
  + complete assembly and plan lineage remain retained beside the digest
  + root-only and mixed known vectors, independent reference bytes, sensitivity tests, global tests, audit, and recursive evidence are proven
  + physical origin, enumeration completeness, temporal order, repeat equality, quiescence, receipt, admission, and effects remain absent

& [SupportDelta] exposes a supplied pair-comparison seam
  + [closed] one exact digest identity for one complete supplied ordered sequence
  + [still_open] whether two complete output-only digest carriers use a comparable scope
  + [still_open] whether both retained carriers still rederive exactly under current authority
  + [still_open] one explicit equal or different disposition over comparable digest subjects
  + [still_open] exact retention of both complete inputs and side-qualified nested faults
  + [still_open] physical acquisition order, elapsed interval, stable process state, enumeration completeness, Git reconciliation, receipt issuance, and admission

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] activate the physical scanner
    - rejected because safe traversal, per-entry owned-handle provenance, enumeration completeness, further Win32 calls, and M2D fixture authority remain unsigned
  + [candidate_B] construct TopologyReceipt directly
    - rejected because physical root binding, scanner policy, nonce and time semantics, issuer identity, repeat-observation evidence, and receipt authority remain absent
  + [candidate_C] compare two bare SHA-256 strings
    - rejected because bare text can bypass output-only lineage, current rederivation, encoding-profile identity, scope correlation, and capability limits
  + [candidate_D] treat digest equality as quiescence
    - rejected because two equal supplied values contain no proof of physical origin, observation order in time, process ownership, external-writer absence, or atomic snapshot
  + [candidate_E] reconcile two complete supplied ordered-inventory digest carriers
    + consumes exactly two output-only WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest values by value
    + retains both complete carriers in one private Serialize-only result
    + rederives each carrier from its retained plan and assembly under current authority
    + requires exact current profiles, encoding profile, scan limits, and root scope identity
    + emits equal or different as an ordinary closed disposition rather than treating difference as a transform fault
    + produces no physical, temporal, quiescence, receipt, admission, or effect claim

& [SelectedBoundary] is supplied ordered topology inventory digest reconciliation
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest-reconciliation/0.1
  + [target_module] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_ordered_topology_inventory_digest_reconciliation.rs
  + [input] is exactly two completed WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest carriers and never plans, assemblies, observations, or digest strings alone
  + [plan] has exact profile and one nonzero reconciliation identity for caller correlation only
  + [current_rederivation] clones each retained digest plan and assembly, invokes the proven digest transform, and requires exact result equality
  + [scope] requires exact digest and encoding profiles, exact TopologyScanLimits, root relative path, root kind, root volume serial, and root file identity
  + [disposition] is equal only when both lowercase ordered_inventory_sha256 values are byte equal, otherwise different
  + [output] retains plan, left carrier, right carrier, common scope account, and disposition behind private fields
  + [faults] distinguish JSON, profile, identity, left digest, right digest, scope profile, limits, root scope, resource, and internal failures

& [RoleVocabulary] prevents temporal laundering
  + [left] and [right] identify supplied operands only
  + [equal] means equal canonical encoded observation sequences under the exact common encoding profile except for ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + [different] means the two comparable supplied sequence commitments are unequal
  + [comparable] means current output-only provenance, profile, limits, and root-scope gates pass
  + [stable] is forbidden because no observation time or physical lifecycle is present
  + [before] and [after] are forbidden because caller order is not independently observed here
  + [double_inventory] is reserved for a future physical protocol that proves two actual inventory acquisitions and binds their order
  + [quiescent_double_inventory] is reserved for a still later lifecycle gate with process and external-writer accounting

& [ScopeComparison] is strict but narrow
  + exact TopologyScanLimits prevent equal sequences collected under incomparable capability ceilings from being silently treated as one comparison
  + exact root relative path, kind, volume serial, and 128-bit file identity prevent cross-root digest comparison from becoming ordinary drift
  + assembly_identity, commitment_identity, projection identities, entry-reference identities, and carrier-only proof lineage remain correlation or provenance roles and do not decide semantic sequence equality
  + entry count, total file bytes, individual paths, kinds, metadata, streams, content digests, and ordinals are already committed by the ordered digest and may differ normally
  + no path normalization, case folding, sorting, repair, semantic field comparison, or canonical-byte exposure is added

& [RevalidationBoundary] composes existing authority
  + each supplied digest is output-only and therefore already construction-gated
  + rederivation nevertheless protects current use against future type evolution, stale retained correlations, or incorrect downstream shortcut assumptions
  + rederived result must equal the complete supplied carrier, not merely its digest string
  + left and right nested failures remain side qualified and no partial reconciliation result is released
  + the reconciliation module may call the proven public digest transform but may not duplicate or widen its canonical encoder

& [EvidenceGrade] is comparable supplied sequence pair only
  + [supplied] both operand lineages remain caller supplied at their original boundaries
  + [output_only] neither bare digest nor raw assembly input is admitted
  + [current_rederived] both complete digest carriers match fresh pure derivation
  + [scope_correlated] exact limits and root identity are common
  + [pair_equal_or_different] only the two canonical sequence commitments are compared
  + [physically_ordered_temporally_stable_quiescent_double_inventory_receipted_admitted] absent

& [RequirementDelta] is proposed M2B-SOTIDR-001 through M2B-SOTIDR-013
  + [authority_state] unprocessed_source_not_yet_preserved
  + [effect_state] zero

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - no filesystem, Windows call, handle, pointer, unsafe, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, Git command, fixture, traversal, physical inventory, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion
  - no bare digest overload, raw assembly overload, direct private-field construction, serializer hash, field-by-field repair, inferred time order, stability claim, quiescence claim, or receipt construction
  - stop if scope equality and semantic sequence equality are collapsed into one meaning
  - stop if different is treated as a malformed input fault rather than a valid comparison disposition

& [Decision] is continue only through source preservation and governing SJS before implementation
  + [next] preserve the selected boundary byte-exactly as a new raw source document
  + [then] run full SJS explosion, semantic refinement, constraints, pruning, seven-fold exhaustion, data design, justification, plan, registry, matrix, slice, phase lock, and satisfaction signature
  + [implementation_authority] absent until that signature exists
  + [physical_authority] absent
